      "title": "Components and state",
      "description": "**New idea — component:** a function that returns what to show on screen. `ChatPage` is one.\n\n**New idea — state:** `React.useState(...)` gives a component a value it remembers between renders, plus a function to change it. `const [providers, setProviders] = React.useState<Provider[]>([])` means: start with an empty list, and call `setProviders` to change it.\n\n**New idea — hooks:** functions whose names start with `use` (`useUser`, `useState`) are hooks. Call them at the top of a component, never inside an `if` or a loop.\n\n**How it works:** when you call a setter, React **runs the component again** and updates the screen.\n\n**Why it matters:** this is how the screen changes when data arrives. You never edit the page directly.\n\n**Watch out:** `_fetchAttempted` is set but never read. A leading underscore is the convention for *intentionally unused*."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/app/(authenticated)/chat/page.tsx",
