          "line": 37,
          "character": 72
        }
      },
      "title": "useEffect: doing work after render",
      "description": "**New idea — effect:** `useEffect` runs code **after** the component appears on screen. It's the right place to fetch data.\n\n**How it works:** the effect defines an `async` function and calls it. That function gets your login token, then calls `/api/providers` through `authFetch`, which adds the token to the request.\n\n**Why it matters:** this is how the chat page learns which ad accounts you've connected.\n\n**Watch out:** the effect function itself can't be `async`. That's why the code defines `fetchProviders` inside it and calls it near the end (line 71)."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/app/(authenticated)/chat/page.tsx",
      "line": 53,
