        "end": {
          "line": 53,
          "character": 40
        }
      },
      "title": "Turning API data into app data",
      "description": "**What it is:** reshaping the API's reply into the `Provider` type the UI uses.\n\n**How it works:** `.map(...)` builds a new object for each provider. AdMob accounts keep a `publisherId`; Ad Manager (`gam`) accounts keep a `networkCode`. Then `setProviders(...)` stores the list, and React re-renders.\n\n**Why it matters:** the UI never depends on the raw API shape, so the API can change without breaking every component.\n\n**Watch out:** on a 401 (token not ready yet), it just returns and waits. The effect runs again when your user data updates, which is the next step."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/app/(authenticated)/chat/page.tsx",
      "line": 73,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 69,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 73,
          "character": 44
        }
      },
      "title": "The dependency list",
      "description": "**New idea — dependencies:** the array at the end of `useEffect` lists the values it depends on. React runs the effect again whenever one of them changes.\n\n**How it works:** here that's `getAccessToken`, `isUserLoading` and `user`. When your login finishes loading, `user` changes and the effect runs again, this time with a token.\n\n**Why it matters:** this is how the 401 case in the last step fixes itself.\n\n**Watch out:** an empty array `[]` means *run once*. No array at all means *run after every render*, a common cause of endless loops."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/app/(authenticated)/chat/page.tsx",
      "line": 85,
