          "character": 95
        }
      },
      "title": "Conditional rendering and props",
      "description": "**New idea — conditional rendering:** a component can return different things. While the user loads, this one returns only a spinner.\n\n**New idea — props:** `<ChatContainer providers={providers} isLoadingProviders={isLoading} />` passes data **down** to a child component. The child can read props but not change them.\n\n**Why it matters:** the page fetches the data and the container shows it. Each component has one job.\n\n**Watch out:** `key=\"new-chat\"` is a special prop. When a key changes, React throws the old component away and starts fresh. As the comment says, that resets the chat when you go from a saved chat back to **/chat**."
    },
    {
