      },
      "title": "State vs refs",
      "description": "**New idea — refs:** `useRef` also remembers a value, but changing it does **not** redraw the screen.\n\n**How it works:**\n- `messages`, `isLoading` and `currentSessionId` are **state**, because the screen depends on them.\n- `abortControllerRef`, `currentStreamIdRef` and `currentAssistantIdRef` are **refs**: background bookkeeping, read with `.current`.\n\n**Why it matters:** the abort controller lets the **Stop** button cancel a running request. It must be remembered, but there's nothing to show on screen.\n\n**Watch out:** if a value appears on screen, it must be state. If you keep it in a ref, the screen won't update when it changes."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/components/chat/chat-container.tsx",
