        }
      },
      "title": "Custom hooks",
      "description": "**New idea — custom hooks:** you can write your own `use…` functions to move logic out of a component.\n\n**How it works:** the container uses three:\n- `useChatSession` creates a chat in the database and saves messages.\n- `useChatApprovals` tracks tools waiting for your Allow or Deny.\n- `useChatPersistence` restores the chat from the browser's storage after a reload.\n\n**Why it matters:** your project's rule (in `CLAUDE.md`) is *components render UI, hooks handle logic*. That keeps this 579-line component from growing even bigger.\n\n**Watch out:** hooks can take functions and refs as inputs. `useChatApprovals` receives `setMessages`, so it can update the chat from outside the component."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/hooks/chat/useChatSession.ts",
      "line": 37,
