        }
      },
      "title": "Inside a custom hook",
      "description": "**What it is:** one custom hook, up close.\n\n**How it works:** it returns two functions. `createSession` sends a POST to `/api/chat/session` and returns the new chat's id. `saveMessage` stores one message.\n\n**New idea — useCallback:** wrapping a function in `useCallback` keeps the **same** function between renders, unless its dependencies (`getAccessToken`, `selectedOrganizationId`) change.\n\n**Why it matters:** stable functions stop effects and child components from re-running for no reason.\n\n**Watch out:** this hook sends the token in a header called `x-stack-access-token`, while most other calls use `Authorization: Bearer`. It's a legacy name, and the API accepts both."
    },
