      "title": "Context: sharing without passing props",
      "description": "**New idea — context:** some data is needed almost everywhere, like who's logged in. Instead of passing it through every component as props, React lets you put it in a **context** that any component below can read.\n\n**How it works:** `UserProvider` (line 85) puts the user, the token helper and the organisation into `UserContext`. `useUser()` reads it. If a component calls `useUser()` outside the provider, it throws a clear error.\n\n**Why it matters:** any component can call `useUser()` to get the token. That's how the chat page got `getAccessToken`.\n\n**Watch out:** when a context value changes, every component reading it re-renders. That's why big apps split context into several smaller ones."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/components/providers/index.tsx",
      "line": 60,
