      },
      "title": "The provider stack",
      "description": "**What it is:** every app-wide context, nested like layers of an onion. The root layout wraps every page in this.\n\n**How it works**, from outside to inside:\n1. PostHog: product analytics\n2. React Query: caching for API data\n3. Neon Auth UI: login screens and the session\n4. Demo mode and demo experiments\n5. User: the `useUser()` data\n6. Entity data: your accounts and apps\n7. Theme: light or dark\n\n**Why it matters:** order matters, because an inner provider can use an outer one. `UserProvider` reads the session from Neon Auth, so it sits inside it.\n\n**Watch out:** the `Suspense` with `fallback={null}` (line 52) means that while something inside loads, nothing is shown rather than a spinner."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/components/chat/chat-container.tsx",
      "line": 189,
      "selection": {
