          "line": 189,
          "character": 115
        }
      },
      "title": "useMemo: remembering calculations",
      "description": "**New idea — useMemo:** `useMemo(() => value, [deps])` remembers a calculated value and only recalculates it when the deps change.\n\n**How it works:** the container works out which accounts are active and enabled, then builds `chatContext`. That's the settings sent to the agent with every message: enabled accounts, model and context mode.\n\n**Why it matters:** without it, these values would be rebuilt on every render, and anything depending on them would think they had changed.\n\n**Watch out:** with the React Compiler switched on (tour 02), much of this would happen automatically. The hand-written versions still work."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/components/chat/chat-input.tsx",
      "line": 436,
      "selection": {
