          "line": 436,
          "character": 13
        }
      },
      "title": "JSX and Tailwind",
      "description": "**New idea — JSX:** the HTML-like code inside a component. It turns into JavaScript. Two differences from HTML: `className` instead of `class`, and `{ }` for JavaScript values.\n\n**How it works:**\n- `className={cn(...)}` combines Tailwind classes. Each class is one small style: `px-4` is horizontal padding, `text-sm` is small text, `max-h-[200px]` is a custom height limit.\n- `contentEditable` makes a plain `div` editable. It's used instead of a textarea so accounts can appear as inline badges when you type `@`.\n- `data-testid=\"chat-input\"` lets the Playwright tests find this box.\n\n**Why it matters:** you can now read any component: logic at the top, JSX at the bottom.\n\n**Watch out:** editable divs are fiddly. Pasting, cursor position and empty states all need custom code, which is a big part of why this file is 601 lines."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/components/chat/chat-container.tsx",
      "line": 520,
