      },
      "title": "Passing a function down",
      "description": "**New idea — lifting state up:** the input box doesn't send messages itself. The container passes it a function, `onSend={handleSendMessage}`, and the input calls it.\n\n**How it works:** data flows **down** as props (`isLoading`, `providers`), and events flow **up** through functions (`onSend`, `onStop`).\n\n**Why it matters:** the container owns the chat state, so it's the only place that changes it. That makes the flow easy to follow, and tour 04 traces it.\n\n**Watch out:** `disabled={!hasProviders}` greys out the input until you connect an ad account."
    },
    {
      "title": "What you can do now",
      "description": "### What you can do now\n\n- Read a component: props in, state and effects inside, JSX out.\n- Tell state from refs, and say when an effect runs again.\n- Follow data down (props) and events up (functions).\n- Say where shared data lives (context) and where logic lives (custom hooks).\n\n**Next:** *04 - Sending a message*. It follows your typed message from the input box to the agent server."
    }
